   "source": [
    "# SPY intraday momentum: baseline and confirmation variation\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements a core subset of Zarattini, Aziz and Barbon (2025), *Beat the Market: An Effective Intraday Momentum Strategy for S&P500 ETF (SPY)*. It evaluates whether unusually large intraday movements continue, and whether waiting for two consecutive signals improves a baseline strategy.\n",
    "\n",
    "The hypothesis is that persistent buying or selling pressure can produce trends. This notebook measures price signals; it does not directly observe order imbalances or establish their causal role. Momentum can fail when breakouts reverse or prices move sideways.\n",
    "\n",
    "The baseline corresponds to the paper's current band + VWAP stop with 100% sizing (paper Table 2, second row: Sharpe 1.24 over 2007-2024), not to its dynamically leveraged headline result. The implementation uses fixed 1x entry sizing instead of the paper's dynamic volatility targeting. Both strategies use the same data, chronological split, costs and execution assumptions. Rules were fixed before evaluating the final test period. This is an educational backtest, not a full replication or live trading system.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Running the notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "Open in Google Colab and run cells in order. If needed, install `requests pandas numpy matplotlib` first. The downloader requests a Massive API key privately with `getpass`. Do not enter a key in saved source code. Existing raw CSVs under `data/` are reused; remove them only if intentionally refreshing the dataset. Local Jupyter users can run from the repository root after installing `requirements.txt`.\n",
    "\n",
  
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Data access\n",
    "\n",
    "Massive REST API provides unadjusted SPY minute OHLCV, daily OHLCV and cash dividends for 1 November 2024–30 September 2026. Downloads are monthly, follow pagination, and respect request limits. Saved outputs contain 185,525 minute rows, 478 daily rows and eight dividend records. The paper used IQFeed over a much longer period, so identical performance is not expected.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-09T02:07:01.504364Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-09T02:07:01.504035Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-09T02:07:01.967235Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-09T02:07:01.966572Z"
    },
    "id": "I5Z6CMuHH7e9",
    "outputId": "5383d937-e65c-403b-d640-d83570440991"
   },
   "outputs": [
