   "source": [
    "## 2. Data checks and indicators\n",
    "\n",
    "Prices must be positive, OHLC relationships consistent, volumes nonnegative, timestamps unique, and values present. Timestamps use America/New_York to handle daylight saving.\n",
    "\n",
    "Five sessions without all 390 regular-session minute bars are excluded. Their dates are printed below. Final reporting treats these sessions as zero-return cash days. Whole-day completeness screening is retrospective: scheduled early closes can be known beforehand, but unexpected missing bars cannot. A production system would require a causal missing-data policy. Sessions absent entirely from minute data should also be investigated against the daily calendar.\n",
    "\n",
    "At each minute, sigma is the mean absolute movement from the day's open at that same minute over the preceding 14 retained complete sessions. It is **not a standard deviation**. Shifting the history by one day excludes the current session. The first 14 complete sessions are warm-up only.\n",
    "\n",
    "Upper band = max(today's open, previous close minus today's ex-dividend amount) × (1 + sigma). Lower band = min(the same anchors) × (1 − sigma). VWAP resets daily and approximates trade-level VWAP using minute typical price (high + low + close)/3 weighted by volume. Raw prices are used, avoiding double dividend adjustments.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this dataset, all five excluded sessions are scheduled early closes (13:00 close, 211 bars each): 29 Nov 2024, 24 Dec 2024, 3 Jul 2025, 28 Nov 2025 and 24 Dec 2025. These dates are known in advance, so excluding them does not use future information, and no unexpected missing bars were found. None of them falls in the final test period.\n"
   ]
  },
