   "source": [
    "## 5. Trading engine and risk controls\n",
    "\n",
    "Start each evaluation with $100,000. At completed decision bars, buy when close > max(upper band, VWAP); short when close < min(lower band, VWAP); otherwise the signal is flat. A long exits when the long condition no longer holds, and a short exits when the short condition no longer holds. Equality causes an exit. Baseline reversals close one position and open the opposite position, charging both transactions.\n",
    "\n",
    "Check entries and exits at 10:00, 10:30, …, 15:30 New York time. API bars are start-labelled: the 09:59 bar completes at 10:00, and execution is proxied by the 10:00 bar's open. This excludes future signal-bar information but assumes no processing delay; executable fills are not guaranteed. End-of-day liquidation uses the 15:59 minute close as a 16:00 fill proxy. **This is a modelling assumption:** the previous close used for the bands comes from the daily file (the official close), and it differs from the 15:59 bar close by about $0.07 per share on average (more than $0.05 on 46% of days). A closing-auction order would fill near the official close instead. The headline results keep the 15:59 proxy; section 14b reports the effect of the alternative as a labelled sensitivity, not as a replacement.\n",
    "\n",
    "Entry notional plus entry costs is capped at account equity, using whole shares. Shares stay fixed until exit, so notional exposure can drift above 1x as prices change. Positions close daily and cannot overlap. Short positions are assumed available and executable; borrowing/margin restrictions are not modelled.\n",
    "\n",
    "Commission is $0.0035/share/side; slippage is $0.001/share/side, deducted as a monetary cost. Reversals incur costs on both orders. These are paper-based assumptions, not a complete current brokerage fee schedule. Minimum order fees, other fees, borrowing charges and interest are omitted. Half-hour exits do not provide continuous protection between checks.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-09T02:07:10.361785Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-09T02:07:10.361516Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-09T02:07:10.371624Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-09T02:07:10.370631Z"
    },
    "id": "uHj-EaszLjmY"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_backtest(\n",
    "    data,\n",
    "    confirmation_required=1,\n",
    "    initial_equity=100_000,\n",
    "    commission=0.0035,\n",
    "    slippage=0.001,\n",
    "    official_close=None,\n",
    "):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    confirmation_required=1: baseline\n",
    "    confirmation_required=2: our confirmation variation\n",
    "\n",
    "    Costs are dollars per share, per side.\n",
    "    Slippage is deducted as a monetary execution cost.\n",
    "\n",
    "    official_close: None (default, used for all headline results) exits at the\n",
    "    15:59 bar close. A {date: price} dict exits at the official daily close\n",
    "    instead; this is used only for the labelled sensitivity in section 14b.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    equity = float(initial_equity)\n",
    "    daily_records = []\n",
    "    trade_records = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for date, group in data.groupby(\"date\", sort=True):\n",
    "        day = group.sort_values(\"timestamp\").reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "        starting_equity = equity\n",
    "\n",
    "        position = 0       # 1 = long, -1 = short, 0 = flat\n",
    "        shares = 0\n",
    "        entry_price = None\n",
    "        entry_time = None\n",
    "        entry_cost = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "        previous_signal = 0\n",
    "        consecutive_signals = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "        def close_position(exit_price, exit_time, reason):\n",
    "            nonlocal equity, position, shares\n",
    "            nonlocal entry_price, entry_time, entry_cost\n",
    "\n",
    "            gross_profit = (\n",
    "                position * shares * (exit_price - entry_price)\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            exit_cost = shares * (commission + slippage)\n",
    "\n",
    "            # Entry costs were already deducted when entering.\n",
    "            equity += gross_profit - exit_cost\n",
    "\n",
    "            trade_records.append({\n",
    "                \"date\": date,\n",
    "                \"direction\": \"long\" if position == 1 else \"short\",\n",
    "                \"entry_time\": entry_time,\n",
    "                \"exit_time\": exit_time,\n",
    "                \"shares\": shares,\n",
    "                \"entry_price\": entry_price,\n",
    "                \"exit_price\": exit_price,\n",
    "                \"gross_pnl\": gross_profit,\n",
    "                \"costs\": entry_cost + exit_cost,\n",
    "                \"net_pnl\": gross_profit - entry_cost - exit_cost,\n",
    "                \"exit_reason\": reason,\n",
    "            })\n",
    "\n",
    "            position = 0\n",
    "            shares = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "        for i in range(len(day) - 1):\n",
    "            row = day.iloc[i]\n",
    "\n",
    "            # Massive timestamps label the START of a minute bar.\n",
    "            # The 09:59 bar is completed at 10:00.\n",
    "            decision_time = row[\"timestamp\"] + pd.Timedelta(minutes=1)\n",
    "            clock_minutes = decision_time.hour * 60 + decision_time.minute\n",
    "\n",
    "            if not (\n",
    "                600 <= clock_minutes <= 930\n",
    "                and clock_minutes % 30 == 0\n",
    "            ):\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "\n",
    "            price = row[\"close\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "            if price > max(row[\"upper_band\"], row[\"vwap\"]):\n",
    "                signal = 1\n",
    "            elif price < min(row[\"lower_band\"], row[\"vwap\"]):\n",
    "                signal = -1\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                signal = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "            # Count consecutive scheduled signals.\n",
    "            if signal == 0:\n",
    "                consecutive_signals = 0\n",
    "            elif signal == previous_signal:\n",
    "                consecutive_signals += 1\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                consecutive_signals = 1\n",
    "\n",
    "            previous_signal = signal\n",
    "\n",
    "            # Execute AFTER observing the completed signal bar.\n",
    "            next_row = day.iloc[i + 1]\n",
    "            execution_price = float(next_row[\"open\"])\n",
    "            execution_time = next_row[\"timestamp\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "            # Exit if the current position no longer meets its rule.\n",
    "            if position != 0 and signal != position:\n",
    "                close_position(\n",
    "                    execution_price,\n",
    "                    execution_time,\n",
    "                    \"band/VWAP exit\",\n",
    "                )\n",
    "\n",
    "            # Enter when flat and confirmation is sufficient.\n",
    "            if (\n",
    "                position == 0\n",
    "                and signal != 0\n",
    "                and consecutive_signals >= confirmation_required\n",
    "            ):\n",
    "                if equity <= 0:\n",
    "                    raise RuntimeError(\"Account equity is non-positive.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "                # Allow room for entry costs within 1x account value.\n",
    "                shares = int(\n",
    "                    equity / (execution_price + commission + slippage)\n",
    "                )\n",
    "\n",
    "                if shares > 0:\n",
    "                    position = signal\n",
    "                    entry_price = execution_price\n",
    "                    entry_time = execution_time\n",
    "                    entry_cost = shares * (commission + slippage)\n",
    "\n",
    "                    equity -= entry_cost\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Scheduled end-of-day liquidation.\n",
    "        # Final minute close is a proxy for the session-close fill.\n",
    "        if position != 0:\n",
    "            final_row = day.iloc[-1]\n",
    "            final_price = (\n",
    "                float(final_row[\"close\"])\n",
    "                if official_close is None\n",
    "                else float(official_close[date])\n",
    "            )\n",
    "\n",
    "            close_position(\n",
    "                final_price,\n",
    "                final_row[\"timestamp\"] + pd.Timedelta(minutes=1),\n",
    "                \"end of day\",\n",
    "            )\n",
    "\n",
    "        if equity <= 0:\n",
    "            raise RuntimeError(\"Account equity is non-positive.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        daily_records.append({\n",
    "            \"date\": date,\n",
    "            \"starting_equity\": starting_equity,\n",
    "            \"equity\": equity,\n",
    "            \"daily_return\": equity / starting_equity - 1,\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "    daily_results = pd.DataFrame(daily_records).set_index(\"date\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    trade_columns = [\n",
    "        \"date\", \"direction\", \"entry_time\", \"exit_time\",\n",
    "        \"shares\", \"entry_price\", \"exit_price\",\n",
    "        \"gross_pnl\", \"costs\", \"net_pnl\", \"exit_reason\",\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    trades = pd.DataFrame(trade_records, columns=trade_columns)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Accounting check: all daily profits should match trade profits.\n",
    "    total_profit = equity - initial_equity\n",
    "    assert np.isclose(total_profit, trades[\"net_pnl\"].sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "    return daily_results, trades"
   ]
  },
