  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Original variation: two-signal confirmation\n",
    "\n",
    "Require matching nonzero signals at two consecutive half-hour decision times before entering. For example, matching signals at 10:00 and 10:30 permit entry at 10:30. Confirmation resets each day and whenever the signal becomes flat or changes direction. Exits and all other assumptions remain unchanged.\n",
    "\n",
    "Expected edge: waiting may filter temporary breakouts and reduce turnover. Tradeoff: a 30-minute delay may miss profitable trend movement and reduce remaining holding time. This is a single prespecified variation, not a search for the best historical parameters.\n"
   ]
  },
