   "source": [
    "## 8. Performance definitions\n",
    "\n",
    "Use net daily account returns, including zero-return days. Annualized return is compounded growth: (ending/starting equity)^(252/N) − 1. Annualized volatility is sample daily standard deviation × sqrt(252). Sharpe is mean daily return / daily standard deviation × sqrt(252), assuming a zero risk-free rate. Annualization is a reporting convention, not a forecast.\n",
    "\n",
    "Maximum drawdown measures the decline from previous peaks using daily closing equity, including starting capital. It can miss larger intraday drawdowns. A tiny positive arithmetic-mean Sharpe can coexist with negative compounded growth because they summarize returns differently.\n",
    "\n",
    "Earlier tables below use eligible sessions. The final table later includes excluded sessions as cash days and is authoritative.\n"
   ]
  },
