   "source": [
    "## 11. Buy-and-hold and common evaluation calendar\n",
    "\n",
    "Buy SPY at the first test session's daily open and hold until the last daily close, charging the same per-share cost assumptions on purchase and sale. Hold dividends as cash without reinvesting. Dividends are credited on ex-date rather than payment date, a simplifying assumption; a purchase on an ex-date receives no dividend for that date. Splits are not explicitly handled, so raw-price use requires checking corporate actions for the chosen period.\n",
    "\n",
    "Include every session from the daily dataset between evaluation endpoints. On excluded sessions the intraday portfolios remain in cash. The benchmark remains invested. Neither earns interest on cash. This is a comparator with different overnight exposure and risk, not proof of equivalence between strategies.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
